.TH RUSTFETCH 1 "September 2026" "rustfetch 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustfetch \- blazingly fast system information fetch tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustfetch
prints system information (OS, kernel, hardware, desktop environment, and more)
alongside an ASCII or image logo. It aims for fastfetch parity with a pure-Rust
implementation, JSON/JSONC configuration, themes, and an interactive setup TUI.
.PP
By default, empty info modules are hidden in human-readable output (useful on
containers and VMs). Use
.B \-\-show\-empty
or set
.B display.showEmpty
in the config to show blank keys.
.B \-\-json
always includes null/empty fields.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-setup, \-\-themes, \-\-theme\-picker, \-\-tui
Launch the interactive full-screen theme and layout setup TUI.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Use a theme once without saving it to the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-set\-theme " NAME"
Save a theme as the default in the config file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
List available color themes and layouts.
.TP
.B \-\-preview\-themes
Print a live preview of every theme.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo " NAME"
Specify a custom distro or OS logo.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo\-color " COLOR"
Override the logo primary ANSI color.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo\-type " TYPE"
Logo type:
.BR kitty ,
.BR kitty\-direct ,
.BR kitty\-icat ,
.BR sixel ,
.BR iterm ,
.BR file ,
.BR builtin ,
or
.BR auto
(auto probes
.BR TERM ,
.BR TERM_PROGRAM ,
.BR KITTY_WINDOW_ID ,
.BR ITERM_SESSION_ID ,
and related env vars).
.TP
.BI \-\-kitty " PATH"
Display an image logo using the Kitty graphics protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-kitty\-direct " PATH"
Display an image using direct Kitty file transfer.
.TP
.BI \-\-kitty\-icat " PATH"
Display an image via
.BR kitten\ icat .
.TP
.BI \-\-sixel " PATH"
Display an image logo using the Sixel graphics protocol (PNG/JPEG; WezTerm, foot, Windows Terminal where supported, and other sixel terminals).
.TP
.BI \-\-iterm " PATH"
Display an image logo using the iTerm2 inline image protocol (OSC 1337).
.TP
.BI \-\-logo\-width " NUM"
Width in terminal cells for image logos.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo\-height " NUM"
Height in terminal cells for image logos.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo\-padding " NUM"
Horizontal padding between logo and module lines.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logo
Hide the ASCII distro logo.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI terminal colors.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " MODE"
Color output mode:
.BR always ,
.BR auto ,
or
.BR never .
.TP
.BI \-\-structure " LIST"
Colon- or comma-separated list of modules to display
(for example
.BR title:os:kernel:cpu:memory:colors ).
.TP
.BI \-\-disk\-paths " PATHS"
Comma-separated mount paths to check (default:
.BR / ).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to a custom JSON/JSONC configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-gen\-config
Print the default JSON configuration to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-import\-fastfetch " [PATH]"
Import a fastfetch JSON/JSONC config into rustfetch.
If
.I PATH
is omitted, searches
.B ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc
and
.BR ~/.config/fastfetch/config.json .
Writes to
.B ~/.config/rustfetch/config.jsonc
(or
.BR \-\-config ).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing rustfetch config when importing.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the mapped import to stdout without writing a file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-logos
List all supported distro and OS logos.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-modules
List all available information modules.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output system information in structured JSON format.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-empty
Show info modules even when their value is empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " SHELL"
Print a shell completion script to stdout.
.I SHELL
must be
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
or
.BR fish .
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print version information.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.
.SH MODULES
Common modules include
.BR title ,
.BR os ,
.BR kernel ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR memory ,
and
.BR colors .
Run
.B rustfetch \-\-list\-modules
for the full catalog.
.PP
Scriptable modules:
.TP
.B command
Run a process and use trimmed stdout as the value. Config keys:
.BR key ,
.BR command
(or fastfetch\-style
.BR text ),
optional
.BR shell
(boolean),
.BR timeout
(milliseconds, default 1500),
and
.BR showFailure .
Failures and timeouts produce an empty value (hidden unless
.B \-\-show\-empty
or
.B showFailure ).
.TP
.B custom
Static text. With
.B key
and
.B text ,
prints a keyed info line. With only
.B format ,
prints a decorative structural line.
.PP
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/rustfetch/config.jsonc
Default configuration file (JSON with comments allowed).
.TP
.B ~/.config/rustfetch/themes/
Directory for user-defined theme JSONC files.
.TP
.B ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc
Default location searched by
.B \-\-import\-fastfetch
when no path is given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive setup:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-setup
.fi
.TP
One-shot theme:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-theme groups
.fi
.TP
Import a fastfetch config (dry-run):
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-import\-fastfetch ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.TP
Import and overwrite the rustfetch config:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-import\-fastfetch \-\-force
.fi
.TP
Show empty modules:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-show\-empty
.fi
.TP
JSON output:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-json
.fi
.TP
Generate bash completions:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/rustfetch
.fi
.TP
Custom module structure without logo:
.nf
.B rustfetch \-\-no\-logo \-\-structure title:os:kernel:cpu:gpu:memory:colors
.fi
